      "_template": "imageTextLeft",
      "image": {
        "src": "/media/commonsense/common-sense-2.webp",
        "alt": "Common Sense 2"
      },
      "title": "CommonSense",
      "subtitle": "Creating the symbol",
      "copy": "The symbol is constructed from two interlocking circular rings, starting with two identical circles whose centres are placed on the edge of the other, creating an intersection at the centre. These circles are transformed into thick rings, and specific sections are cut or removed to give the impression that the rings are interwoven.\n\nThe construction lines highlight the intersections that define the final shapes, resulting in a symmetrical and visually balanced design that suggests interconnectedness, unity and infinite cycles."
    },
